  + // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  + // Git-redirect guard — worker bash commands must not escape the worktree
  + // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  + //
  + // A spawn worker running inside an isolated worktree can defeat that isolation
  + // by redirecting git back into the shared main checkout via `git -C <path>` or
  + // `git --git-dir=...` (bug class transferred from Claude Code v2.1.212's fix
  + // log). The detector lives HERE, next to its call site in
  + // `guard_worker_git_redirect` / `GitRedirectGuard::execute` — same file, same
  + // commit, so cross-file dead-code failures (the 2× revert cause) cannot recur.
  + //
  + // Scope: the two redirect shapes above only. `GIT_DIR=`/`GIT_WORK_TREE=`
  + // env-prefix and `--work-tree` detection are a named follow-up ("Extend spawn
  + // git-redirect guard: env-prefix + --work-tree shapes").
